# Production secrets for the VPS deployment (deploy/setup-vps.sh and
# deploy/redeploy.sh read this file) — copy to .env.prod (gitignored) and fill
# in real values. Never commit .env.prod.
#
# For local development on your Mac you want server/.env instead; this file is
# only for the live VPS.

DOMAIN=api.yourdomain.com
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
FAST2SMS_API_KEY=
FAST2SMS_OTP_ID=

# --- Driver KYC image storage (S3-compatible) ---------------------------
#
# Driver selfies, Aadhaar and licence photos. Object storage rather than the
# VPS filesystem: a rebuild must not take every driver's documents with it,
# and re-collecting them is not something drivers will do twice.
#
# Set up on Cloudflare R2 (no egress fees, S3 API):
#   1. R2 -> Create bucket, e.g. "sarthi-driver-documents". Keep it PRIVATE —
#      nothing here is ever served publicly.
#   2. R2 -> Manage API tokens -> Create token, Object Read & Write, scoped to
#      that one bucket.
#   3. S3_ENDPOINT is https://<account-id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
#
# Any S3-compatible service works; for AWS S3 leave S3_ENDPOINT empty and set
# S3_REGION to the bucket's real region.
S3_BUCKET=
S3_REGION=auto
S3_ENDPOINT=
S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# --- At-rest protection for personal numbers ----------------------------
#
# DOCUMENT_ENCRYPTION_KEY encrypts driver bank account numbers (payouts need
# the number back, so it cannot be hashed). Exactly 32 bytes, base64:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
#
# DOCUMENT_HASH_PEPPER keys the fingerprint that detects the same Aadhaar
# registered twice. Aadhaar numbers themselves are never stored, only this
# fingerprint and the last 4 digits:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
#
# Losing DOCUMENT_ENCRYPTION_KEY makes every stored account number
# unrecoverable, and changing DOCUMENT_HASH_PEPPER invalidates every existing
# Aadhaar fingerprint. Back both up somewhere other than this server.
DOCUMENT_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
DOCUMENT_HASH_PEPPER=
